content.text:
I’ve fixed the slice boundary. This PR will:

- create one durable refund record for the immutable cancellation-history row, using its exact recorded amount;
- execute or recover that refund idempotently against the captured PaymentIntent;
- keep the booking cancelled if Stripe is unavailable, showing a truthful pending/failed state with a retry action;
- show successful refund status on the profile and exercise the real cancellation journey through the guarded Playwright provider.

Refund webhooks, receipts, and broader operations tooling remain later #75 slices. That keeps this PR end-to-end without absorbing the rest of the epic. I’m creating the feature branch and starting with failing service/provider/action/UI tests.

